## §16 — Future Direction: Control Plane, Update Factory, Research Pipeline

Per ADR-0052, future-direction positioning leads with deterministic replay and
evidence integrity. Air-gap remains a supported topology, but not the headline.
Replay never re-inferences regardless of whether the original inference topology
was cloud-only, local-only through RamaLama, or hybrid.

Per ADR-0038 / ADR-0039 / ADR-0040 / ADR-0041 / ADR-0042 / ADR-0043, Zovark's
architecture extends beyond the Customer Instance to a fleet-management
Control Plane, an Update Factory producing two-distinct-role-signed
reproducible bundles, and a Research Pipeline generating improvement
candidates under gated promotion. These subsystems are **not** built in M1; M1
only ensures the architecture cannot drift away from these decisions during
M2-M10. The autonomy boundary (INV-030) — Research Pipeline output is never
customer-runtime authoritative until promoted by the Update Factory and
accepted by customer policy — is the single most important rule.

zvadmin (described in §11) is the **customer's** operator console for managing
their own Zovark instance. It is **not** the Control Plane (which is Zovark's
fleet management). They are different subsystems with different infrastructure,
different authentication models, and different data classifications.

ADR-0043 (open-source release strategy) is currently `PROPOSED-STRATEGIC-PIVOT`
pending founder sign-off (tracked as M1-DECISION-001 in DD_BLOCKERS.md). Until
sign-off, the runtime-code licensing posture is not finalized; the schemas
remain Apache-2.0 per ADR-0010.

